# Documentation

- `AGENTS.md` is canonical for agent rules; tool files (`CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.cursor/rules/`) only add tool-specific delivery and must not duplicate or contradict it.
- Use relative links; check that every link target exists.
- Do not create empty or duplicate documents; extend the existing one that owns the topic (see `docs/README.md`).
- Requirement IDs (FR/NFR), task IDs (T-x.y) and ADR numbers are stable; deprecate instead of renumbering.
- Accepted ADRs are not edited in place; write a superseding ADR.
- Mark unvalidated statements as **[validate]**; never present assumptions as facts.
